<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Hume returns three weeks after presenting with looser stools, dark blood, tiredness, and iron deficiency anemia. Colonoscopy thirteen days ago reached the cecum and found a 4 cm ulcerated mass at 28 cm in the sigmoid colon, which was biopsied and tattooed; there were no other lesions. The biopsy shows moderately differentiated adenocarcinoma with intact mismatch-repair proteins. The staging CT eleven days ago showed two small pericolic lymph nodes, clear lungs, and one 9 mm indeterminate lesion in the liver. He still has two or three loose stools a day with dark blood on some days, and he tires on hills. His weight is down a further 0.8 kg. He saw Dr. Mehta of medical oncology this morning and has a colorectal surgery appointment this week. He took the news calmly and asked for the facts plainly; he wants to keep working on his books. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Diagnosis confirmed by biopsy; staging CT done</td></tr><tr><td>Bowel symptoms</td><td>Two or three loose stools a day; dark blood on some days</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>Down 0.8 kg in three weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Tires on hills; working at his desk each morning</td></tr><tr><td>Coordination</td><td>Medical oncology seen today; colorectal surgery this week</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

