<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Adenocarcinoma of the sigmoid colon, clinical stage T3 N1, metastasis not yet excluded (C18.7)</content>. Biopsy-proven, mismatch-repair proficient. CEA 6.4 ng/mL is raised and will be the baseline for surveillance. Liver tests are normal. The 9 mm liver lesion is too small to characterize on CT and must be clarified before surgery, because a metastasis would change the plan. [S]<list><item>MRI of the liver with contrast in three days, as Dr. Mehta advised.</item><item>Colorectal surgery appointment this week for laparoscopic sigmoid colectomy if the liver lesion is benign.</item><item>Plan adjuvant treatment after the surgical pathology is known.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Iron deficiency anemia from tumor blood loss (D50.0)</content>. Hemoglobin 10.3 g/dL with ferritin 9 ng/mL at presentation. Surgery is about two weeks away, too soon for oral iron to work. [S]<list><item>Ferric carboxymaltose 750 mg intravenously today and again in one week.</item><item>Blood count and ferritin six to eight weeks after the infusion, at the postoperative visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>CEA, preoperative baseline</td><td>Once before resection</td><td>Completed today</td><td>6.4 ng/mL, raised</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Liver tests at staging (ALT, AST, alkaline phosphatase, bilirubin)</td><td>At staging</td><td>Completed today</td><td>All normal</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Hemoglobin before intravenous iron</td><td>Before treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>10.3 g/dL</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>CT of the chest, abdomen, and pelvis</td><td>At staging</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Done eleven days ago: two pericolic nodes up to 7 mm, clear lungs, one indeterminate 9 mm liver lesion</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>MRI of the liver</td><td>When CT shows an indeterminate liver lesion</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Booked in three days</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Complete colonoscopy before resection</td><td>At diagnosis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Reached the cecum thirteen days ago; no other lesions, so the first surveillance colonoscopy will be due one year after resection</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Mismatch-repair testing of the tumor</td><td>At diagnosis, for every colorectal cancer</td><td>Up to date</td><td>MLH1, PMS2, MSH2, and MSH6 intact on the biopsy (mismatch-repair proficient)</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Medical oncology</td><td>At diagnosis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seen this morning; recommendations in the consultation note</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Colorectal surgery</td><td>At diagnosis</td><td>Referred</td><td>Appointment this week</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Intravenous iron infusion</td><td>Each dose</td><td>Completed today</td><td>First 750 mg dose given with 30 minutes of observation; no reaction</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Blood count and ferritin after intravenous iron</td><td>6 to 8 weeks after infusion</td><td>Due</td><td>At the postoperative visit</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Distress and depression screen (PHQ-2)</td><td>At each follow-up visit</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Not done today, the visit at which the diagnosis and plan were discussed, a deviation from the CMID schedule. He appeared composed and asked for plain facts; screening is added to the postoperative visit</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Complete diagnosis, staging, and curative resection within six weeks of presentation. In progress; target 2026-07-13 [S]</item><item>Replete iron stores before surgery and recover hemoglobin by the postoperative review. In progress; target 2026-07-13 [S]</item><item>Complete three months of adjuvant CAPOX with neuropathy no worse than grade 1. In progress; target 2026-10-19 [S]</item><item>Start survivorship surveillance with a written survivorship care plan. In progress; target 2026-10-19 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Colon Cancer, Version 4.2025 (2025); AGA Clinical Practice Guidelines on the Gastrointestinal Evaluation of Iron Deficiency Anemia (2020); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, colorectal cancer and anemia monographs (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: MRI of the liver in three days. Second iron infusion in one week. Colorectal surgery this week. Primary care review about four weeks after surgery. Next scheduled visit 2026-07-13: review four weeks after laparoscopic sigmoid colectomy, before adjuvant chemotherapy. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
